# preview — a preview is built with dryRun(), which is the only renderer in
# internal/cmd that consults --json (INVARIANTS.md H-2, second half).
#
# This is a VIOLATION surface, not a census: internal/surfaceaudit.PreviewSurface
# lists only the --confirm-gated entrypoints that assemble their preview some
# other way. Empty is the goal, and it is empty. The extractor is guarded
# against silently matching nothing by TestPreviewExtractorFlagsAHandRolledPlan,
# which feeds it a known-bad function, rather than by a non-empty check.
#
# It was not empty. Nine previews were prose under --json — svc call, script
# run, script apply, auto apply, dash replace and the three wireguard
# mutations — while the enforcement H-2 cited, TestPreviewJSONIsMachineReadable,
# exercised `helper create` and nothing else.
#ceiling 0
